[
  {
    "id": "1344a63230580090",
    "text": "Auto tool changing is one of the key features of Carvera and also the base of all the automated function. Please test it at the first time.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/carvera/manual/unpack"
  },
  {
    "id": "30a15c376d270a6c",
    "text": "1. Open the control software and connect to Carvera.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/carvera/manual/unpack"
  },
  {
    "id": "11ef3d3f5a56ab76",
    "text": "2. Change to tool 1. The tools that pre-installed in the machine is tool 6. Click tool status; click “Change…”; choose “Tool: 1”, it will automatically change to tool 1. Please observe the process to see if there is any error.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/carvera/manual/unpack"
  },
  {
    "id": "1ff43a4943366c70",
    "text": "3. Change to wireless probe. If no error occurred, then test wireless probe. Click tool status; click “Change”; select “Probe”, it will automatically change to wireless probe and check its signal. Please observe the process to see if there is any error.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/carvera/manual/unpack"
  },
  {
    "id": "7657e41a1e2d1442",
    "text": "4. Change back to tool 1. Please follow step 2.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/carvera/manual/unpack"
  },
  {
    "id": "30050265dcd4fdfc",
    "text": "Note: If you decide not to use Carvera for a long time, please keep a tool clamped in the spindle, but do not use the wireless probe. It will reduce the elasticity of the tool clamp without a tool for long time. The wireless probe cannot be charged automatically if it is not in the tool holder.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/carvera/manual/unpack"
  },
